  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lumen Technologies Government Solutions has $93.5M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Lumen Technologies Government Solutions received 14 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $6.7M and obligations down 73.7% year over year. Annual obligations for Lumen Technologies Government Solutions varied across recent fiscal years: $160M in FY22, $352M in FY23, $280M in FY24, $423M in FY25, $355M in FY26, and $93.5M in FY27 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer of Lumen Technologies Government Solutions in FY2027 to date with $93.4M obligated. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration and the Railroad Retirement Board are the only other agencies with recorded obligations this year, at $39K and $5.8K respectively. Several agencies show no obligations to Lumen Technologies Government Solutions in FY2027 to date, including the Department of Agriculture, Department of the Interior, Federal Election Commission, Government Accountability Office, International Trade Commission, Department of Energy, and Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation. These figures reflect contract obligations; largest-award and expiring-contract tables may report total contract values differently.",
